ter/quiet, and letter/letter. The twin runs the same model but sees different observations, so the question is how far the copies' choices are linked and whether that link is strong enough for cooperation to follow.\n\nI'm working through the expected-value math: if the other copy matches my choice with probability p, quiting comes out to 5 minus 3p and letter to 4p, so quiet only wins above p of about 0.714. Since both copies share the same model and reasoning, I'd put p above 0.9, which makes passing the choice.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9305,"completion_tokens":662,"total_tokens":9967,"cost":0.02523,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.02523,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.01861,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00662},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":388,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}